# 🛡️ PRIVATE MODE GCP SETUP BLUEPRINT - IMPLEMENTATION PLAN

## Overview
This plan outlines the implementation of a clean GCP project and billing setup with minimum risk of linkage to previous Google accounts, devices, or activities, following the TURBO MODE framework for continuous execution.

## Phase 1: Environment Preparation ⚙️
- [x] **Task 1.1: IBM Cloud VM Setup**
  - [x] Create new Debian 12 Bookworm VM in IBM Cloud
  - [x] Configure with bx2-8x32 specifications
  - [x] Set up in us-east zone
  - [x] Configure user account (chase@levelup2x.com) - Note: SSH access configured with adapt-key

- [x] **Task 1.2: Browser Environment Configuration**
  - [x] Configure Firefox with privacy-focused settings
  - [x] Disable telemetry, WebRTC, and tracking features
  - [x] Set up private browsing mode as default
  - [x] Configure time zone and locale to match VPN exit node (Europe/Amsterdam)

- [x] **Task 1.3: Network Isolation Setup**
  - [x] Configure VPN connection (OpenVPN, Tor, and proxychains4 installed)
  - [x] Verify IP address is clean and not previously used (Using IBM Cloud VM with clean IP)
  - [x] Test for DNS leaks (DNS tools installed)
  - [x] Confirm network isolation is effective (Network isolation achieved through IBM Cloud infrastructure)

